@startuml
' Domain model, version 1. Transcribed from the team's domain diagram.
' Version 1 only has human Players, so Player has no subtypes yet.
' The original diagram draws X, O and Empty as kinds of Color; here Color is an enum with those three values.
title Tic-Tac-Toe — domain model (version 1)
hide empty members

class TicTacToe
class Board
class Round
class Player
class Square
class Coordinate
class Piece
enum Color {
  X
  O
  EMPTY
}
class Goal
class Win
class Put

TicTacToe *-- "1" Board
TicTacToe *-- "1" Round
TicTacToe *-- "2" Player
Round --> "2" Player : alternates
Player --> Board
Player o-- Color
Player o-- Goal
Goal <|-- Win
note bottom of Win : Row, Column,\nDiagonal, Inverse Diagonal
Goal ..> Put
Goal ..> Square
Board *-- "3x3" Square
Square o-- "0..1" Piece
Put ..> Square : target
Put ..> Coordinate
Put ..> Piece
Piece *-- Coordinate
Piece *-- Color
@enduml
